\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Post-training protocol family}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{post-training}

\p{A \strong{post-training protocol family} is a declared collection of
procedures that begin with a base policy and produce a new policy from
task-facing data. A member specifies which records it can acquire, which
objective it evaluates, and which parameter transition it applies.}

\p{This is an \strong{FTIP synthesis}, not a definition copied from one
paper. The supervised, reward-model, and PPO stages summarized in
\citet{Sections 3.1 and 3.5}{ouyang2022training} give one composition. The
reinforcement-learning stages in \citet{Section 2}{guo2025deepseek} give a
different composition.}

\p{The family is part of the claim. Two studies do not describe the same
intervention merely because both call their last stage post-training.}
